  "riseState": {
    "open": true,
    "grade": "reconstructed",
    "text": "\n    Barrel rise (m)1.0286254881847008\n    \n      \n      Why Not a measured vault rise. Preserve the former reconstructed gable peak: half of the shorter unchanged 3.05 m plan span times tan(34 degrees) = 1.02862548818 m above the unchanged 2.6 m wall. The old 34-degree gable parameter is no longer a visitor-facing pitch claim: a curved roof has varying tangent. A circular segment across the unchanged 4.51 m front, the existing 0.30 m projection and 0.07 m covering edge are working reconstructions, not dimensions read from Whistler or Currey. Covering, material and colour remain the existing reconstruction; the black-and-white illustration attests none of them.\n      No source is named for this one.\n    \n  ",
    "note": "Why Not a measured vault rise. Preserve the former reconstructed gable peak: half of the shorter unchanged 3.05 m plan span times tan(34 degrees) = 1.02862548818 m above the unchanged 2.6 m wall. The old 34-degree gable parameter is no longer a visitor-facing pitch claim: a curved roof has varying tangent. A circular segment across the unchanged 4.51 m front, the existing 0.30 m projection and 0.07 m covering edge are working reconstructions, not dimensions read from Whistler or Currey. Covering, material and colour remain the existing reconstruction; the black-and-white illustration attests none of them."
